Tundra: E-commerce order lifecycle

  Roles:
    - Customer
    - Merchant
    - Payment Provider

  Relationships:
    - Customer is Owner of Cart
    - Customer is Owner of Order
    - Merchant is Handler of Order

  Contracts:
    - Only a Customer may add items to a Cart or place an Order
    - An Order may be placed only from a Cart that contains at least one item
    - Payment must succeed before an Order can move to Paid
    - Only the Merchant may mark an Order as Shipped or Delivered
    - A Customer may cancel an Order only while it is in Placed or Paid state
    - Once an Order is Shipped it can no longer be cancelled by the Customer

  States:
    - Cart is Empty
    - Cart has Items
        @contains LineItems
        @quantity at least 1
    - Order is Placed
    - Order is Paid
    - Order is Shipped
    - Order is Delivered
    - Order is Cancelled
    - Order is Payment Failed

  Processes:
    - Add item to Cart
    - Remove item from Cart
    - Place Order
        @quantity at least 1
    - Capture Payment
    - Fail Payment
    - Mark as Shipped
    - Mark as Delivered
    - Cancel Order
        @before Shipped

  Scenario: Happy path – customer buys and receives goods
    Given the Cart is Empty
    When the Customer adds an item to the Cart
    Then the Cart has Items

    When the Customer places the Order
    Then the Order is Placed

    When the Payment Provider captures payment successfully
    Then the Order is Paid

    When the Merchant marks the Order as Shipped
    Then the Order is Shipped

    When the Merchant marks the Order as Delivered
    Then the Order is Delivered

  Scenario: Error – payment fails
    Given the Order is Placed
    When the Payment Provider fails to capture payment
    Then the Order is Payment Failed

  Scenario: Error – customer tries to cancel after shipping
    Given the Order is Shipped
    When the Customer tries to cancel the Order
    Then the cancellation is rejected
    And the Order remains Shipped
    And the contract "Once an Order is Shipped it can no longer be cancelled by the Customer" is broken

  Scenario: Error – place order from empty cart
    Given the Cart is Empty
    When the Customer tries to place an Order
    Then the order is rejected
    And the contract "An Order may be placed only from a Cart that contains at least one item" is broken
